-- Q11306: Government Regulation of Business [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Section 12(a)(2) of the Securities Act of 1933, any person who offers or sells securities by means of a prospectus containing a material misstatement is liable to the purchaser. The remedy is rescission or damages, and scienter (intent to deceive) is not required.
Wrong (A): Section 12(a)(2) provides civil remedies to purchasers; criminal prosecution is a separate action pursued by the DOJ, not a remedy available to individual investors.
Wrong (B): Section 12(a)(2) does not require proof of intent to deceive; liability attaches upon proof of a material misstatement in the offering materials.
Wrong (D): Section 12(a)(2) does not require the investor to demonstrate specific reliance on the misstatement; purchasing through the defective prospectus is sufficient.$EXPL$
