-- Q11308: Government Regulation of Business [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under SEC Rule 506(b) of Regulation D (17 CFR Section 230.506(b)), general solicitation or general advertising is strictly prohibited as a condition of the exemption. The sales agent''s telephone solicitations to 50 unknown individuals constitute general solicitation, violating this requirement regardless of whether any purchases resulted. Loss of the exemption exposes the entire offering to Section 5 registration violations.
Wrong (A): The unqualified investor''s misrepresentation of net worth is a separate issue; the general solicitation violation independently destroys the exemption.
Wrong (B): Rule 506(b) prohibits the conduct of general solicitation itself, not just resulting sales; unsuccessful solicitations still violate the rule.
