  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Section 16(b) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, any profit realized by a statutory insider (director, officer, or 10%+ shareholder) from a purchase and sale within six months must be disgorged to the company. Chen''s profit is $150,000 (10,000 shares x $15 gain). Section 16(b) is strict liability requiring no proof of insider trading intent.
Wrong (A): Directors are expressly included as statutory insiders subject to Section 16(b) disgorgement; they are not exempt.
