  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 56(a)(1), real property placed in service after 1998 uses the same straight-line method for both regular tax and AMT purposes, so no adjustment is required. The AMT depreciation adjustment primarily affected pre-1999 assets where different methods or periods applied.
Wrong (A): No accelerated AMT method applies to real property placed in service after 1998; the 150% declining balance method is not required.
