UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Sections 55 and 59(j), a child subject to the kiddie tax computes AMT on the child''s own return using the child''s own exemption and preference items. The $8,000 PAB interest is Parker''s AMT preference under Section 57(a)(5) and must be reported on Parker''s Form 6251.
Wrong (B): The kiddie tax rate substitution does not eliminate AMT exposure; AMT is a separate parallel computation regardless of how regular tax rates are applied.
