-- Q11330: Alternative Minimum Tax [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 55(b)(2), AMTI begins with regular taxable income, to which AMT adjustments (Section 56) and tax preference items (Section 57) are added or subtracted. The computation starts after all regular deductions have been applied.
Wrong (A): AGI is an intermediate figure in the regular tax computation; the AMT calculation starts with taxable income, which is after deductions are applied to AGI.
Wrong (B): Gross income is too early in the computation; it precedes both above-the-line deductions and itemized/standard deductions.
Wrong (D): ''Total income before exemptions'' is not a defined term in the IRC; AMTI begins with regular taxable income as computed on the return.$EXPL$
