-- Q11331: Alternative Minimum Tax [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 55(b)(1), the AMT exemption is subtracted from AMTI to determine the base on which AMT rates (26% and 28%) are applied. It functions as a flat reduction of the taxable base, sheltering a portion of AMTI from the AMT rate.
Wrong (B): The AMT exemption is a base reduction subtracted before computing tax, not a dollar-for-dollar credit applied against the resulting tax liability.
Wrong (C): The exemption reduces AMTI itself, not specific preference items; it does not eliminate or target particular preference categories.
Wrong (D): The standard deduction is an AMT adjustment added back to AMTI; the AMT exemption is a separate and distinct concept that reduces the AMT base.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11331;
